Styling an HTML page with CSS can be hard at first, so here are the basics to get started:

First you need to create an HTML file and a CSS file. In this example, the HTML file will be called index.html and the CSS file style.css.
Inside index.html, you will need to import the CSS file to be able to use it. To do so, add the following line inside your <head> </head> tags inside your index.html file.
```
<link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css">
```

- every CSS field should have either a tag, and ID or a class, followed by brackets. It should look like so:
```
p {

}
