Regular HTML tags are accessed by simply putting their name. 
HTML classes are accessed from CSS by using a dot (.) in front of the name. 
HTML IDs are accessed from css by using a hashtag (#) in fron of the name.

Here is an example showing all three CSS tags:
```
/* Regular HTML tag, can be anything in HTML. For example, a <div> would be the following*/
